window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sejuani","b":"zaahen","win":["Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"He starts out-trading a tank with no kill pressure — concede the trades, keep the farm."},{"when":"Zaahen level 3","text":"The Darkin Glaive and Aureate Rush are both 10s — step up only when both are down."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Grim Deliverance is 110s — bait it, then R-into-Permafrost is your equaliser."},{"when":"Grouped mid game","text":"Your engage value dwarfs his the moment fights stop being 1v1s."}],"wants":{"you":["Safe farm and untouched scaling","CC chains landed with jungle help","Teamfights instead of sidelane duels"],"foe":["Repeated 1v1 trades in lane","Dreaded Return pulling you into him","A sidelane where his damage grinds you down"]},"early":"Accept the lane for what it is: after an even level 1 he out-trades you from 2, and by 3 The Darkin Glaive and Aureate Rush both refresh in 10 seconds while Arctic Assault takes 18. Watch the attack wind-up, not the cast — his Q is a reset. Farm with Q as a disengage, hold your stuns for ganks, and scale.","mid":"At 6 the stage evens on one hinge: Grim Deliverance is 110 seconds and heals him, so bait it and a full R-into-Permafrost chain strips his all-in before it starts — whoever commits CC first takes the exchange. Buy Grievous Wounds early; his Q heals too. After his first item he wins lane trades again.","late":"Late he beats you 1v1 — Aureate Rush scales off health, so stacking bulk does not answer him — so never be in a 1v1. Group early, start every fight with R lockdown, and check his Determination first: filled, Cultivation of War revives him and your 120-second ultimate bought nothing.","whys":["Level 1 is an even skill lane — you are a passive tank and he has no tools online yet.","At 2 he already out-trades a Sejuani who carries no kill pressure of her own.","By 3 The Darkin Glaive and Aureate Rush both refresh in 10s — his windows.","Levels 4-5 stay his: your CC needs setup that he simply denies.","At 6 Grim Deliverance is 110s and heals him; bait it, then R-into-Permafrost strips his all-in — the stage rides on who commits CC first.","His first item keeps him winning lane trades while you scale for fights, not the lane.","Late his damage beats a tank that cannot kill him, and Cultivation of War can revive him — group."]});
